docs/DEVELOPMENT.md --- Text
26 26 The user explicitly authorized expert subagents. Three lanes own Rust authorization, browser UI/E2E and independent security review. Each receives a fresh scope-and-oracle capsule without parent history. The controller owns documentation, package pins, integration and acceptance. Writers have disjoint files and no commit authority; only one fixed-port E2E runs at a time. No acceleration multiplier or financial saving is inferred from parallel work.
27 27
28 28 For 0.4, Best Defaults selects server-enforced action approvals before wider delegation: the baseline demonstrates sensitive writes using only a copied valid session. The implementation reuses the existing WebAuthn handlers and typed action data. The shared contract is STEPUP-CONTRACT.md; the full gate and independent review run on the resulting integrated source. Existing dependencies remain pinned. A failed or canceled browser ceremony can be retried; it cannot authorize an unrelated operation. Remote source equality, a fresh clone and hosted CI status are separate evidence surfaces.
   29
   30 For 0.5, the closed objective is a passkey-approved online delegation chain and transitive revocation at the API execution point. DELEGATION-CONTRACT.md fixes the profile, signing bytes, limits, endpoints and disjoint expert ownership before implementation. Metacode found no fitting delegation donor; existing Ed25519/WebAuthn/SQLite dependencies are reused. The browser lane independently authors a Node standard-crypto encoder and public synthetic vectors; Rust consumes those fixtures and the browser checks actual API-produced signatures. The read-only reference CLI joins both native and portable CI gates. The custom service-attested profile is explicitly separate from UCAN, DIDs and holder-signed offline credentials.

docs/DONORS.md --- Text
 4  4
 5  5 Research used the local `metacode` index first. Its passkey/vault queries returned general Rust registries, with no candidate-specific donor. Candidate decisions therefore use official repository files, package metadata and product documentation. [Projected evidence](evidence/donors-v03.json) records exact versions, commits, integrity and limitations. Repository activity is an observation, not a security audit.
 6  6
 .  7 The 0.5 delegation search likewise found no matching protocol donor. The general awesome-rust source was checked through Metacode; its status does not certify a listed dependency. Existing ed25519-dalek2.2.0 remains the signer/verifier, with standard Node crypto as an independent reference. No UCAN implementation or additional key-vault code is consumed. The [delegation contract](DELEGATION-CONTRACT.md) defines the separate service-attested profile; current primary-source and package evidence is in [v05-donor-research.json](evidence/v05-donor-research.json).
 .  8
 7  9 ## Selected layers
 8 10
